{"name":"Castlegate","hex":"#a0a5a5","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[],"entries":[{"title":"Gate","blocks":[{"text":"A gate or gateway is a point of entry to or from a space enclosed by walls or other barriers. The word is derived from Proto-Germanic *gatan, meaning an opening or passageway. Synonyms include portal. The concept originally referred to the gap or hole in the wall or fence, rather than a barrier which closed it. Gates may prevent or control the entry or exit of individuals, or they may be merely decorative. The moving part or parts of a gateway may be considered \"doors\", as they are fixed at one side whilst opening and closing like one."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/94/Gate_of_the_BCR_Headquarters_Building_%28Bucharest%2C_Romania%29.jpg/330px-Gate_of_the_BCR_Headquarters_Building_%28Bucharest%2C_Romania%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gate"},{"title":"Castlegate, Aberdeen","blocks":[{"text":"Castlegate is a small area of Aberdeen, Scotland, located centrally at the east end of the city's main thoroughfare Union Street. Generally speaking, locals consider it to encompass the square at the end of Union Street where the Mercat Cross and Gallowgate are located."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Aberdeen_Market_Cross.jpg/330px-Aberdeen_Market_Cross.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Castlegate%2C_Aberdeen"},{"title":"Castlegate (York)","blocks":[{"text":"Castlegate is a historic street in York, England, which leads to York Castle."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0a/Castlegate%2C_York_showing_the_spire_of_St_Mary%27s_Church_-_geograph.org.uk_-_886305.jpg/330px-Castlegate%2C_York_showing_the_spire_of_St_Mary%27s_Church_-_geograph.org.uk_-_886305.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Castlegate_(York)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f9/Castel_B%C3%A9ranger%2C_February_16%2C_2013.jpg/500px-Castel_B%C3%A9ranger%2C_February_16%2C_2013.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f9/Castel_B%C3%A9ranger%2C_February_16%2C_2013.jpg/1280px-Castel_B%C3%A9ranger%2C_February_16%2C_2013.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f9/Castel_B%C3%A9ranger%2C_February_16%2C_2013.jpg/500px-Castel_B%C3%A9ranger%2C_February_16%2C_2013.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Art Nouveau gate of Castel Béranger (Paris)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACastel_B%C3%A9ranger%2C_February_16%2C_2013.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a7/Kebun_Raya_Bali_Candi_Bentar_IMG_8794.jpg/500px-Kebun_Raya_Bali_Candi_Bentar_IMG_8794.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a7/Kebun_Raya_Bali_Candi_Bentar_IMG_8794.jpg/1280px-Kebun_Raya_Bali_Candi_Bentar_IMG_8794.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a7/Kebun_Raya_Bali_Candi_Bentar_IMG_8794.jpg/500px-Kebun_Raya_Bali_Candi_Bentar_IMG_8794.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Candi bentar, a typical Indonesian gate that is often found on the islands of Java and Bali","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AKebun_Raya_Bali_Candi_Bentar_IMG_8794.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/75/Torii_de_Miyajima_2.JPG/500px-Torii_de_Miyajima_2.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser